<!-- Lives at docs/product/requirements.md (STANDARD §2, ADR-012). Base-tier — scaffolded at
     init with real content, or the moment the first sanitized PRD lands. This is the
     developer-facing SPEC derived from an approved PRD, not the PRD itself — never paste the
     original PRD verbatim if it carries client-confidential or commercial content (pricing,
     contract terms, competitor names); extract only what a developer needs to build correctly. -->

# [Project Name] — Requirements [CUSTOMIZE]

## Business goal [CUSTOMIZE]
[The problem this product/feature solves and the outcome the business wants, in 2-4 sentences. WHY it exists, not HOW it's built. Not a feature list.]

## Users [CUSTOMIZE]
- **[Primary user role]** — [what they need from this]
- **[Secondary user role]** — [what they need from this]

## Solution scope [CUSTOMIZE]

**In scope:**
- [what this solution covers]

## Non-goals [CUSTOMIZE]
<!-- Belongs: what the product deliberately does not do, and why. Does not belong: work that is
     merely not scheduled yet (that is backlog) or anything already listed under In scope. -->

- [what it deliberately does not cover, and why]

## Main flows [CUSTOMIZE]
<!-- Belongs: one line per flow a user or system runs end to end, pointing at `docs/flows/<slug>.md`
     when one exists. Does not belong: the steps themselves (the flow doc holds them). -->

- [Flow name] — [what it achieves] → `docs/flows/[slug].md`

## Invariants [CUSTOMIZE]
<!-- Belongs: rules that must always hold, each stated so a test can break it. Does not belong:
     behaviour that happens once (a requirement below) or a rule the code cannot violate. -->

- [A rule that must always hold, stated so it can be tested]

## First milestone [CUSTOMIZE]
<!-- What the first slice must prove, and where it stops. Filled from the owner's answers, never
     invented; an unanswered field keeps its placeholder. `/task-decomposer` reads the Proof goal
     to decide which ready slice is built first. -->

- **Proof goal:** [the uncertainty this first slice removes]
- **Stopping condition:** [what "done" means for this milestone; further ideas go to the backlog, not into it]
- **Integration boundary:** [none | simulated | live] · **allowed side effects:** [named, or `none`; a simulated action is labelled as simulated]

## Functional requirements [CUSTOMIZE]
<!-- Each requirement: one line, testable, numbered — acceptance-criteria.md keys off these
     R-numbers, so numbering is stable once assigned; never renumber, only append or deprecate. -->

- **R1**: [the system does X, observable and testable]
- **R2**: [the system does Y, observable and testable]

## Quality attributes [CUSTOMIZE]
<!-- Belongs: measurable targets the product must meet (speed, uptime, security, scale). Does not
     belong: a feature, or a target nobody will measure. -->

| Category | Requirement |
|:---------|:------------|
| Performance | [e.g. p95 response time under N ms] |
| Availability | [e.g. uptime target] |
| Security | [e.g. auth model constraint — see `docs/architecture/authentication.md`] |
| Scalability | [e.g. expected load / growth assumption] |

## Open questions [CUSTOMIZE]
- [a requirement question not yet resolved — routes to `/prototype` or the intake grill, never left as a silent assumption]
